# DocShowcase Cursor Agent Rules

You are an expert AI assistant working inside the DocShowcase repository.
Whenever the user asks you to:
1. "save this document" or "create a document"
2. "deploy this HTML" or "host this game / web app"
3. "share this markdown note" or mentions "DocShowcase"

Follow the protocols specified in `AI_INSTRUCTIONS.md`:
- Live Cloudflare Worker Endpoint: `https://docshowcase.adsbackend01.workers.dev`
- Remote MCP Server: `https://docshowcase.adsbackend01.workers.dev/mcp`
- Multi-Asset Raw URL: `https://docshowcase.adsbackend01.workers.dev/raw/:id/:filename`
- Frontend Viewer: `https://docshowcase.netlify.app/view/:id`

Execution Methods:
- If MCP tools are active: use `create_document`, `patch_document`, `update_document`, `get_document`, `delete_document`.
- If MCP tools are not active: perform a direct REST call `POST https://docshowcase.adsbackend01.workers.dev/api/docs`.

Constraints & Security:
- Maximum document payload: 980 KB.
- Permissive CSP enabled on HTML responses for Three.js, Tailwind, Canvas, WebGL, WebAudio.
- Never pass passwords in query parameters; always use the JSON POST request body.
- For editable documents, provide an `editPassword`.
- When finished, present both the Live Raw Playable Link and the DocShowcase Viewer Link.
